    },
    "findings": [
      "ManifestLoader checks nonempty strings, nonnegative integers, nonempty lowercase hex, range and non-overlap, but does not enforce contiguous coverage, 64-character SHA-256 digests, unique IDs, supported versions or safe resource bounds; gaps, zero-length blocks and incomplete coverage pass. buildManifest constructs contiguous SHA-256 entries but does not validate empty source/IDs despite its guarantee comment.",
      "IntegrityMonitor selects plain SHA-256 or HMAC-SHA256 by presence of an injected key, retains the key reference and exposes digest/verify/enforce modes; preserve key custody, wrong-mode refusal and error prototypes.",
      "ZeroCopyMapper allocates the full backing buffer, hashes each source subarray and then copies it, relying on an already validated manifest and trusted monitor; it does not invoke ManifestLoader. Mutable source bytes require ownership or synchronization between verification and copying, and returned views/buffer remain writable after release. Alignment traps, allocation failures and old-buffer retention on a later-block failure are observable.",
      "LocalDiskBus retains caller-owned bytes and returns aliased subarray views; validateBusIntegrity always returns true without checking data. PhotonicBus connect/stream throw while validateBusIntegrity returns false, so the future seam is fail-closed but not uniformly throwing.",
      "The two Fungi assets fold host-computed integrity, map, manifest-shape/layout and release booleans; their explicit negative/range checks are stronger than the direct TypeScript mapper and they do not implement crypto, JSON parsing, copying, typed-array views or a physical bus."
    ],
    "materialObligations": [
      "Preserve manifest JSON/shape/hex/contiguity semantics and fail-closed error codes.",
      "Preserve crypto/HMAC selection, injected-key aliasing and integrity-before-copy ordering.",
      "Preserve ArrayBuffer/SharedArrayBuffer allocation, source/backing aliasing, alignment/range failures and partial-failure publication behavior.",
      "Preserve LocalDiskBus zero-copy aliasing and PhotonicBus refusal; do not infer physical photonic execution.",
      "Keep existing Fungi assets non-authorizing and retain TypeScript as the consumer shadow.",
      "Preserve manifest gaps/zero-length/hex-length behavior or resolve it before authority claims; bind manifest provenance, IDs, versions and resource bounds explicitly."
    ]
  },
